WEBVTT

01:10.361 --> 01:13.448
We're both at the drainage pumping station
and decided to get a drink.

01:13.531 --> 01:15.325
I didn't think he'd get so messy.

01:17.827 --> 01:19.412
You could've just called a taxi.

01:21.414 --> 01:23.249
It's, uh…

01:24.084 --> 01:24.918
Oh?

01:26.169 --> 01:27.295
You're not staying at home?

01:30.840 --> 01:32.300
Oh, yeah.

01:33.259 --> 01:34.594
It's a long story.

01:35.428 --> 01:36.638
It's a long story.

01:40.141 --> 01:42.268
What were you doing?
It's weird for you to be here, too.

01:42.894 --> 01:45.313
It's a long story for me, too.

01:47.023 --> 01:48.733
Are you saying that,
'cause you don't want to answer,

01:48.817 --> 01:49.651
or 'cause you can't?

01:50.318 --> 01:51.694
I can say the same thing, director.

01:53.822 --> 01:54.656
You what?

01:54.739 --> 01:57.283
Most people would send
their drunk co-worker home in a taxi,

01:57.367 --> 01:59.702
but you took him into a motel
and tucked him in.

02:06.042 --> 02:08.378
Past wounds are cut deep.

02:09.712 --> 02:10.547
Mr. Lee.

02:13.299 --> 02:14.968
IMI MOTEL

02:15.051 --> 02:18.096
I didn't expect you to stick around.

02:18.179 --> 02:19.681
Are you heading home?

02:21.057 --> 02:24.435
Just when you think
the wound is healed, something happens,

02:24.519 --> 02:26.146
and you realize it's still raw.

02:26.229 --> 02:28.439
Come again, don't make this
a one-time thing.

02:29.524 --> 02:30.608
Get home safe.

02:46.416 --> 02:49.127
The more memories you gather
where the heart is wounded,

02:49.210 --> 02:51.504
the more frightened you are
of being wounded again.

02:52.505 --> 02:55.717
Like heat that can't dissipate
trapped in a concrete jungle,

02:55.800 --> 02:59.345
you're stuck surrounded by memories,
unhealed wounds.

02:59.429 --> 03:03.099
You feel a breeze you can ride out,
and just when you think you'll get out,

03:03.183 --> 03:05.977
you feel your wound, the breeze dies down.

03:09.856 --> 03:14.736
EPISODE 6
HEAT ISLAND PHENOMENON

03:14.819 --> 03:17.739
Today, we're reporting
our first heat warning in Seoul this year.

03:17.822 --> 03:20.909
Worsened by heat islands in the city
readmitting heat from the sun,

03:20.992 --> 03:24.412
we know this scorching heat wave
is going to continue for several days.

03:24.495 --> 03:26.497
Heat radiating
from asphalts in the roads,

03:26.581 --> 03:29.042
combined from the heat emitted
from the city's AC units,

03:29.125 --> 03:31.085
are likely raising temperatures
even higher.

03:31.169 --> 03:33.296
More from Reporter Park Cheol-min.

03:42.680 --> 03:45.516
Oh, it's too early to be hot.

03:46.100 --> 03:48.186
Are you really cooking right now?
What are you making?

03:58.279 --> 03:59.948
That time of year already?

04:05.995 --> 04:07.580
Oh, Ma, it's not worth it.

04:07.664 --> 04:09.457
No one eats it, 'cause it's gross.

04:09.540 --> 04:11.376
You're spitting. Go inside.

04:11.459 --> 04:13.419
I'm worried about you staying out here.

04:37.443 --> 04:39.320
It's monsoon season, so he…

04:39.404 --> 04:41.364
he's gonna stay at work
for a little while.

04:41.447 --> 04:43.324
Didn't he come, so he could see us?

04:43.408 --> 04:44.450
Huh?

04:45.994 --> 04:47.704
Well, yes, he did.

04:48.663 --> 04:50.331
- It was just…
- Will he come back?

04:52.625 --> 04:53.710
Uh…

04:55.086 --> 04:56.337
Sure, when the season's over.

05:08.725 --> 05:11.102
Ugh, it's too hot.

05:26.075 --> 05:27.368
Oh, shit.

05:32.623 --> 05:35.626
It's not gonna get any hotter.

05:36.878 --> 05:38.046
Hello.

05:44.844 --> 05:47.013
And the anticyclone
is staying over…

05:47.096 --> 05:48.431
Sorry I'm late.

05:48.973 --> 05:50.558
…still, everyone should stay on the…

05:57.273 --> 05:58.858
And the heat wave

05:58.941 --> 06:01.819
is bringing temperatures above average,
but only temporarily.

06:01.903 --> 06:04.489
- It's warm for June.
- You sure coming early?

06:04.572 --> 06:05.448
Huh?

06:05.531 --> 06:08.284
Does the Team Two
have the night shift starting today?

06:08.910 --> 06:09.786
What today?

06:11.788 --> 06:14.415
It's a lot to keep track off.
Was it very different in Gangwon?

06:15.458 --> 06:17.126
- Goodbye.
- Nice seeing you.

07:13.266 --> 07:15.393
Butter. Butter. Butter. Butter.

07:17.812 --> 07:18.729
Butter.

07:24.402 --> 07:25.736
It smells!

07:38.082 --> 07:42.670
INCOMING CALL
APARTMENT 1302

07:48.092 --> 07:50.386
CALLING
APARTMENT 1201

08:21.542 --> 08:22.627
Coming.

08:24.045 --> 08:26.214
- Oh, you're still here.
- Oh, yeah.

08:26.297 --> 08:27.798
Uh, can I help you with something?

08:27.882 --> 08:29.884
We needed to reach you,
I have texted several times,

08:29.967 --> 08:32.011
maybe you didn't see.
Where are you gonna go?

08:32.094 --> 08:34.597
We got a word that a new trainee
is coming pretty soon,

08:34.680 --> 08:36.682
because of that,
we'd like you to move out.

08:36.766 --> 08:38.518
Ideally, by next week?

08:39.685 --> 08:40.811
Oh, so soon?

08:41.479 --> 08:45.107
There has to be enough time for repairs
and cleaning before they move in.

08:45.191 --> 08:47.693
We had expected you to find a place
after a month.

08:47.777 --> 08:49.153
You didn't know that?

08:49.237 --> 08:50.446
No, no.

08:50.530 --> 08:52.323
Let's plan on that, then. End of the week.

08:52.406 --> 08:54.033
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

09:27.608 --> 09:29.318
Ah, you didn't run
in this weather, did you?

09:30.111 --> 09:32.822
You don't sleep in
even when you're a night shift?

09:35.491 --> 09:36.701
Should I get something to eat?

09:38.661 --> 09:40.121
We should reconsider what we're doing.

09:41.664 --> 09:42.915
Consider what now?

09:43.666 --> 09:44.667
You and me.

09:48.087 --> 09:49.922
"When one cloud meets another,

09:50.006 --> 09:52.550
there's a great noise, thunder.

09:52.633 --> 09:55.136
Like them, I want to meet you,

09:55.636 --> 09:58.806
shouting about it from the rooftops
without a thought.

10:00.683 --> 10:02.768
When one cloud
suddenly meets another cloud,

10:03.311 --> 10:05.771
there's a great light, too, lightning.

10:05.855 --> 10:07.607
With that light when I meet you,

10:07.690 --> 10:10.276
I'll see the path
I strayed from long ago."

10:12.236 --> 10:14.113
Hang on, I don't get the last part.

10:15.031 --> 10:16.157
This stanza.

10:16.240 --> 10:17.700
"You shine like lightning

10:17.783 --> 10:20.286
as you say that a rain cloud
needs to meet another rain cloud

10:20.369 --> 10:21.454
for them to get drenched."

10:21.537 --> 10:22.371
That part.

10:22.913 --> 10:23.873
Hm…

10:25.750 --> 10:30.046
You have to find someone that's like you,
for either of you to open up and rain.

10:31.422 --> 10:32.840
Ah, that's my best guess.

10:33.716 --> 10:34.675
For example?

10:38.471 --> 10:39.597
Let it rain.

10:39.680 --> 10:41.390
What was that?

10:41.891 --> 10:44.226
- You're cloud?
- The pain we've been though,

10:45.519 --> 10:47.313
that's what the poem was describing.

10:49.190 --> 10:52.902
"A rain cloud needs to meet another
for them to get drenched."

10:56.030 --> 10:57.365
What? Why now?

11:01.786 --> 11:04.747
Well, I thought I'd recovered.
I was wrong. I'm not.

11:08.709 --> 11:12.963
All last night, I couldn't stop thinking
about the motel when I saw you.

11:14.131 --> 11:16.384
I keep thinking
of ignoring red flags again.

11:16.967 --> 11:18.135
It's exhausting.

11:20.137 --> 11:22.306
Nothing happened with that woman,
I promise you.

11:22.390 --> 11:26.769
Yeah, and I really wanna believe you.
It'd be better for me.

11:27.395 --> 11:30.648
But I get this feeling in my stomach
every time I think about it.

11:34.026 --> 11:36.821
I know you're not the kind of person
who would lie.

11:36.904 --> 11:39.198
And then that's a problem, too.

11:39.865 --> 11:42.034
You've been nothing but honest, and I…

11:42.743 --> 11:44.537
And that's not enough, for some reason.

11:47.373 --> 11:48.332
Director Jin.

11:48.416 --> 11:50.209
We should take some time
to think about it.

11:51.961 --> 11:55.339
It's not anything you did.
I'll figure things out myself.

12:01.804 --> 12:03.389
I'm gonna head out. Enjoy.

12:06.976 --> 12:08.102
It was my dad.

12:11.564 --> 12:12.898
I only went to the motel…

12:15.860 --> 12:17.069
because I was looking for him.

12:25.870 --> 12:26.746
Mr. Lee?

12:27.538 --> 12:29.373
Lee Myung-han here. I'm his son.

12:34.378 --> 12:35.546
Go ahead.

12:37.715 --> 12:40.009
Hey, why don't you just fold?

12:40.634 --> 12:42.511
It's like looking at a statue.

12:43.137 --> 12:43.971
Come on.

12:44.847 --> 12:46.557
- Shit!
- Hey, pal.

12:46.640 --> 12:47.975
Your boy is here.

12:48.684 --> 12:51.020
He's very handsome.

12:51.103 --> 12:53.689
Oh, Si-woo. You're here.

12:54.982 --> 12:56.233
Hey.

12:56.317 --> 12:57.443
Hey, Si-woo!

12:57.943 --> 12:59.320
Hey, S-woo. Si…

12:59.403 --> 13:01.864
Damn it. Oh! Get back here, Si-woo!

13:01.947 --> 13:03.407
Hey! Hey!

13:03.491 --> 13:05.326
Wait! Wait! Come on!

13:05.409 --> 13:07.328
Si-woo, come on.

13:08.496 --> 13:10.080
Don't walk away from me.

13:10.164 --> 13:11.999
You came all the way here
just to turn around?

13:12.082 --> 13:13.209
You're gambling again?

13:13.292 --> 13:15.795
So this is why you're blowing up my phone,
calling me non-stop?

13:16.754 --> 13:19.590
I had to. You're my only son. Come on.

13:19.673 --> 13:22.009
So, give me all the money
that you brought.

13:25.012 --> 13:26.055
What?

13:26.138 --> 13:27.348
Oh, jeez.

13:27.431 --> 13:29.225
You forgot to bring any?

13:30.434 --> 13:32.770
- Don't have any.
- I know what you do.

13:32.853 --> 13:35.189
Don't lie to me.
I know you landed a big promotion.

13:35.272 --> 13:37.233
You're rolling in cash. I know.

13:37.316 --> 13:41.362
You already burned through
everything I saved from last year.

13:42.363 --> 13:43.197
Did I really?

13:44.198 --> 13:46.784
Well, you know, I'm okay with coins, okay?
Anything works.

13:47.535 --> 13:49.537
Oh, come on. They're gonna
make me dig my own grave.

13:49.620 --> 13:51.288
I'm dying right now, so…

13:51.372 --> 13:53.332
- Just…
- Hey, I don't have any money!

13:53.415 --> 13:56.669
I had to over stay at the training center,
because I can't afford a deposit!

13:56.752 --> 13:58.170
Then get a loan.

13:58.254 --> 13:59.880
If you work for the government,

13:59.964 --> 14:02.383
you're supposed to get lots
of extra stuff.

14:04.009 --> 14:05.636
Don't ever call. I'm done with you.

14:05.719 --> 14:07.304
Contact me and I'll call the police.

14:07.388 --> 14:10.307
I'll never think about you again.
You're not my father any longer.

14:10.391 --> 14:11.934
You little…

14:12.017 --> 14:14.144
Hey, don't go. Stop.

14:14.228 --> 14:15.938
Ungrateful… Huh?

14:17.022 --> 14:18.148
Shit.

14:19.108 --> 14:20.150
Jeez.

14:23.654 --> 14:24.864
What were you doing?

14:25.614 --> 14:27.241
It's weird for you to be here, too.

14:28.492 --> 14:31.203
It's a long story for me, too.

14:32.788 --> 14:34.832
Are you saying that,
'cause you don't want to answer,

14:34.915 --> 14:35.875
or 'cause you can't?

14:36.625 --> 14:38.210
I can say the same thing, director.

14:40.379 --> 14:41.630
She's a director.

14:43.883 --> 14:44.967
You what?

14:45.676 --> 14:48.012
Most people would send
their drunk co-worker home in a taxi,

14:48.679 --> 14:50.598
but you took him into a motel
and tucked him in.

16:29.989 --> 16:31.156
The record's office?

16:32.157 --> 16:33.826
- Why?
- Hm?

16:34.618 --> 16:35.661
For our marriage license.

16:36.495 --> 16:38.664
It's filled out,
we just have to turn it in,

16:38.747 --> 16:41.500
then we're eligible for a housing loan
as a married couple.

16:42.418 --> 16:43.585
Uh-huh.

16:44.461 --> 16:46.880
And you don't want to renew our lease
for the apartment?

16:46.964 --> 16:49.258
It's out of the budget and no amenities.

16:50.092 --> 16:51.010
Mm.

16:56.056 --> 16:57.683
Okay, what's wrong?

16:59.935 --> 17:01.103
You didn't…

17:03.480 --> 17:05.232
get attached to that apartment already.

17:06.650 --> 17:07.609
Guess I did.

17:08.277 --> 17:09.862
Oh…

17:11.405 --> 17:12.364
Yu-jin.

17:13.615 --> 17:16.410
Our home is anywhere we can be together.

17:16.493 --> 17:18.037
That's what matters. It'll grow on you.

17:18.912 --> 17:21.373
I'll find us somewhere really nice,
I promise you.

17:23.917 --> 17:27.004
Right. I'll send you with my seal
and ID card,

17:27.087 --> 17:29.298
and you can turn everything in
for both of us?

17:29.381 --> 17:30.799
I wish I could go, too.

17:30.883 --> 17:32.843
But I've gotta get
my column done for tomorrow.

17:32.926 --> 17:35.095
- Is that okay?
- Sure.

17:35.179 --> 17:36.180
That's great.

17:41.393 --> 17:42.936
- Want mine as well?
- Hm?

17:44.188 --> 17:45.647
You barely touched it.

17:45.731 --> 17:47.024
Don't you like chicken?

17:50.069 --> 17:52.738
Wow, the drumstick.

17:54.448 --> 17:55.532
Mmm.

18:03.540 --> 18:05.417
- Have you eaten?
- Yes, sir.

18:06.668 --> 18:08.128
- Did you have lunch?
- Oh, yeah.

18:09.088 --> 18:11.715
There's a lot to do today,
so gimbap works for me.

18:11.799 --> 18:17.262
Hey, now. Gimbap is basically a snack.
Eating enough is more important than work.

18:17.346 --> 18:18.180
Yup.

18:18.764 --> 18:21.266
- So, uh, what are you working so hard?
- It…

18:21.350 --> 18:22.267
It's nothing.

18:22.351 --> 18:23.644
No, come on.

18:24.603 --> 18:27.815
Well, the director asked me
for a column for internal use.

18:28.398 --> 18:30.067
A column? What about?

18:31.318 --> 18:33.237
- About the month.
- About…

18:34.947 --> 18:37.324
What do you mean?
You're writing monthly column?

18:38.784 --> 18:39.952
I asked him to give it a try.

18:40.911 --> 18:42.830
But that's… It's just I write that column.

18:42.913 --> 18:45.582
Well, it's not ready
and we have to send it to print soon.

18:45.666 --> 18:47.668
You're late and there's a deadline.

18:47.751 --> 18:49.962
I needed a backup.
I can't just hope you'll get it done.

18:50.546 --> 18:53.090
I just wanted to proofread it
a little more.

18:53.674 --> 18:55.676
It's basically completely ready to print.

18:55.759 --> 18:57.469
Right then, wrap it up and let me see.

18:58.303 --> 18:59.429
And Min-jun?

18:59.513 --> 19:01.515
Min-jun, I still wanna see yours, too.

19:02.141 --> 19:03.642
I want both columns.

19:03.725 --> 19:06.520
We'll print whichever's better.
I'll decide. All right?

19:09.314 --> 19:11.191
Assistant Director Kim, good luck.

19:12.693 --> 19:14.194
You as well.

19:14.862 --> 19:16.947
- Yeah.
- Good luck to both of you. Hm?

19:18.657 --> 19:20.826
Mr. Han, good luck.

19:20.909 --> 19:23.245
Thanks. You too.

19:29.126 --> 19:30.419
It's fine.

19:31.962 --> 19:35.632
I'll get it done. He'll see.
I'll get it done.

19:36.300 --> 19:39.052
He'll see. All right, let's go.

19:46.143 --> 19:49.229
MARRIAGE CERTIFICATE

19:49.313 --> 19:52.232
WIFE
SEAL OR SIGNATURE

20:15.756 --> 20:17.841
- I'm going home. Goodbye.
- Mm.

20:25.182 --> 20:26.099
That's it.

20:27.684 --> 20:29.228
- You're done?
- Yeah.

20:29.978 --> 20:31.313
Oh, you're not?

20:32.022 --> 20:33.065
Uh…

20:33.565 --> 20:37.069
I still have lots and lots
of, um, other report to get through.

20:37.653 --> 20:39.321
It goes on and on.

20:40.781 --> 20:42.282
Don't worry about me, though. Go home.

20:42.366 --> 20:44.243
Okay.

20:47.371 --> 20:49.581
I'll see you. Tomorrow, then.

20:49.665 --> 20:50.499
Yeah.

20:51.667 --> 20:52.876
Good night.

21:14.273 --> 21:15.774
Oh, you're here early.

21:15.857 --> 21:18.402
I forgot the schedule flipped
and we were night shift.

21:18.485 --> 21:19.820
I was 12 hours early.

21:20.362 --> 21:23.573
Oh, I thought I was late this morning,
so I rushed over here.

21:23.657 --> 21:25.325
And I ran to Team One.

21:25.409 --> 21:27.703
Maybe you should try
to be early to our team meetings,

21:27.786 --> 21:29.788
and go late to theirs instead, okay?

21:31.540 --> 21:34.668
And, hey, you could've just
left me last night when I got drunk.

21:34.751 --> 21:36.211
I'm sure I was a lot.

21:36.295 --> 21:38.839
We're well into monsoon season.
It's hectic.

21:38.922 --> 21:41.174
I couldn't have you out for a day.
We're all hands on deck.

21:41.258 --> 21:43.885
I need you here.
A valued and crucial team member.

21:43.969 --> 21:46.179
Crucial. I'm more of a burden.

21:47.139 --> 21:49.808
- Did you have dinner?
- Not yet. I'm not that hungry.

21:49.891 --> 21:52.477
I'll see you in 30.
Go get something to eat.

21:53.478 --> 21:54.646
Well…

21:59.651 --> 22:00.736
Whoa.

22:01.778 --> 22:02.738
What is it?

22:06.241 --> 22:07.367
What?

22:14.708 --> 22:16.418
Why was he glaring at me?

22:19.338 --> 22:20.464
- Hello.
- Hello.

22:29.806 --> 22:31.183
Hey, I had dinner.

22:36.605 --> 22:39.483
What did I miss? Hm?

22:40.984 --> 22:42.903
The temperature is fairly high

22:42.986 --> 22:44.613
and the radiation is keeping up.

22:44.696 --> 22:45.655
The sun is about to set,

22:45.739 --> 22:48.200
but the temperature is
still 28 degree Celcius.

22:48.700 --> 22:51.411
I think this heat island
could really melt Seoul to the ground.

22:52.204 --> 22:54.456
Do you think the atmospheric flow
will stay constant?

22:54.539 --> 22:55.624
Who's to say?

22:55.707 --> 22:58.710
We can always get rain out of nowhere.
That seems to happen a lot.

23:13.892 --> 23:16.144
Call me now.
Something's wrong with Mom.

23:21.108 --> 23:22.150
Careful.

23:26.655 --> 23:27.697
Oh…

23:38.375 --> 23:41.086
You're telling me she can't call?
I told her you're under the weather.

23:41.169 --> 23:42.712
It's fine.

23:43.630 --> 23:46.049
I think she's on night shift
starting today.

23:46.133 --> 23:49.386
She could text at least. It's selfish.
And she should be worried about you.

23:49.469 --> 23:51.346
You treat her like a child, and she's not.

23:51.430 --> 23:53.473
She's an adult and selfish.

23:53.974 --> 23:56.351
I bet she thinks it's another trick.

23:57.102 --> 24:00.272
"Oh, our mom is sick
and you need to come over right away."

24:04.943 --> 24:05.861
TAE-KYUNG

24:07.612 --> 24:09.823
Do you have anything
on probability of rain tonight?

24:11.324 --> 24:14.202
Wow. Who does she think she is?

24:18.874 --> 24:21.877
SUPPLEMENTARY WEATHER CHART

24:32.554 --> 24:35.140
It's really so quiet.

24:35.223 --> 24:36.475
It can't always be chaos.

24:37.309 --> 24:39.644
There's still a chance
of localized heavy rain.

24:39.728 --> 24:41.354
Stay alert, everyone.

24:41.438 --> 24:42.647
- Okay.
- Sure.

25:11.384 --> 25:13.261
Hey, are you okay?

25:16.181 --> 25:17.015
Huh?

25:17.599 --> 25:18.850
Are you saying something?

25:19.768 --> 25:22.062
It seems like something
is distracting you today.

25:22.145 --> 25:23.063
Oh.

25:23.813 --> 25:26.775
Well, it's just… family stuff.

25:35.075 --> 25:35.909
Honey.

25:37.536 --> 25:41.498
I wanna take the Level Five
technical exam again.

25:55.720 --> 25:57.138
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

26:02.477 --> 26:04.104
- Director Jin.
- Huh?

26:04.187 --> 26:05.605
Should I answer the phone for you?

26:05.689 --> 26:06.815
Oh, no, it's all right.

26:08.066 --> 26:10.193
Director Jin of Team Two speaking.

26:13.280 --> 26:14.322
What?

26:14.406 --> 26:16.950
He's here, ma'am. He says he knows you.

26:17.742 --> 26:19.786
He says it's urgent
and he wants to see you.

26:19.869 --> 26:20.996
What should I tell him?

26:21.580 --> 26:22.747
Ah, of course.

26:22.831 --> 26:23.790
Let me.

26:25.458 --> 26:26.876
Hi. Hello, director.

26:27.377 --> 26:29.754
I'm Lee Myung-han.

26:29.838 --> 26:31.756
Lee Si-woo's my son, you know.

26:37.679 --> 26:40.724
The thing is,
there's lots we gotta discuss.

26:40.807 --> 26:42.559
The stuff you should know
regarding Si-woo.

26:42.642 --> 26:43.560
So can you…

26:44.561 --> 26:47.314
can you spare just ten minutes
of your time to chat?

26:48.565 --> 26:49.691
Okay.

27:10.837 --> 27:13.757
What an ungrateful brat.
Why hasn't she called?

27:38.907 --> 27:40.158
Oh, damn it.

27:55.465 --> 27:57.467
It's fine. No, no, no, no…

28:11.398 --> 28:13.900
Don't… What am I gonna do?

28:28.331 --> 28:29.916
You are Lee Si-woo's father?

28:31.000 --> 28:32.168
Yeah, that's right.

28:33.002 --> 28:34.045
Si-woo's my son.

28:34.754 --> 28:36.506
I see. Hello.

28:38.425 --> 28:40.427
So, what can I do for you?

28:45.557 --> 28:48.601
Actually, I gotta ask you
something important.

28:53.189 --> 28:56.025
Oh, jeez. I don't… I don't know
how to say this to a stranger.

28:57.485 --> 29:01.406
Then again, we're not strangers
it you have something with my son.

29:04.117 --> 29:05.410
What are you referring to?

29:05.493 --> 29:08.371
I'm referring to seeing you and my son…

29:09.289 --> 29:12.000
being close enough
to hit the motel together.

29:17.088 --> 29:17.964
Ah.

29:18.047 --> 29:20.133
I see. You haven't told anyone.

29:21.593 --> 29:23.762
Okay, okay. I get it.

29:23.845 --> 29:25.180
I won't talk too loud.

29:27.974 --> 29:32.896
Anyway, it's true that… that you two
are a couple, aren't you?

29:32.979 --> 29:33.897
Huh?

29:37.817 --> 29:40.153
I know what I saw
at that motel last night.

29:49.329 --> 29:51.623
Sorry, what did you need
to discuss so urgently?

29:51.706 --> 29:52.916
How much cash you got?

29:54.876 --> 29:59.339
Seems to me you outranked my boy,
you're older than him, too, for sure.

29:59.923 --> 30:01.466
And your title sounds real important.

30:01.549 --> 30:05.929
So I'd guess your salary
beats Si-woo's flat out, right?

30:06.513 --> 30:09.098
See, I really need money.

30:09.182 --> 30:11.017
And I needed it yesterday, right?

30:11.100 --> 30:12.936
Would you find it in your heart
to lend me any?

30:33.414 --> 30:34.541
Hey.

30:34.624 --> 30:36.292
Do you know where Director Jin went?

30:36.835 --> 30:39.462
- I think she got a call and walk out.
- I don't know.

30:41.881 --> 30:43.925
- Try calling her if you have to.
- Okay.

30:56.646 --> 30:58.982
TAE-KYUNG

31:06.447 --> 31:08.867
This is the phone
of Director Jin Ha-kyung.

31:10.910 --> 31:11.744
What?

31:31.222 --> 31:33.766
All right, ma'am. Please climb in.

31:35.184 --> 31:37.353
911 EMERGENCY
AMBULANCE

31:42.567 --> 31:44.819
Sir, shouldn't we tell
the director to go home?

31:45.737 --> 31:48.448
She'd never listen to
the assistant director saying she should.

31:52.493 --> 31:54.037
What do you think, Mr. Um?

32:21.689 --> 32:22.815
Director Jin.

32:25.401 --> 32:27.320
I picked up your phone,
'cause your sister called.

32:28.404 --> 32:29.781
She said your mom is really sick.

32:30.365 --> 32:31.449
Here.

32:36.371 --> 32:37.455
You should call them.

32:38.539 --> 32:39.540
Oh.

32:40.041 --> 32:41.584
It's not. She's done this before.

32:41.668 --> 32:43.461
My mom only gets sick
when we've been fighting.

32:43.544 --> 32:44.754
I'm sure she's just fine.

32:45.505 --> 32:47.674
- Let's go.
- They're taking her to the ER.

32:48.591 --> 32:49.550
Seriously?

32:49.634 --> 32:52.387
Your sister called an ambulance,
and she was crying really hard.

32:53.346 --> 32:55.556
I don't think
they're just trying to trick you.

32:58.893 --> 33:01.145
Jin Ha-kyung. Why aren't you here?

33:01.646 --> 33:03.439
I told you Mom's not well.

33:03.523 --> 33:05.817
I know you're mad
about the matchmaker thing.

33:05.900 --> 33:07.402
Do you care about Mom at all?

33:07.485 --> 33:10.613
I thought even you would at least call
and ask how she's doing.

33:16.953 --> 33:20.873
Our mom is dying.
We're gonna be all alone.

33:24.711 --> 33:27.505
- What hospital are they taking her to?
- I don't know.

33:27.588 --> 33:30.174
They just said we're going to
whichever one can be in fastest.

33:30.258 --> 33:31.092
I'll call.

33:31.175 --> 33:33.678
Okay, then. I'm on night shift,
so I'll come when I can.

33:33.761 --> 33:35.888
Did you hear me? Mom is dying!

33:36.764 --> 33:38.975
They need me.
I can't leave until my shift's done.

33:39.058 --> 33:40.977
I don't care! We need you, too!

33:41.060 --> 33:44.313
I can't leave yet.
As soon as the morning team comes.

33:44.397 --> 33:47.108
I can't believe you! Whatever!
I'm hanging up!

33:51.821 --> 33:52.655
Ma'am.

33:54.907 --> 33:56.576
I'm all right. Get back to work.

33:59.287 --> 34:00.329
Director Jin.

34:02.582 --> 34:03.791
Ah…

34:05.376 --> 34:08.421
I just checked,
since anticyclone's maintaining position,

34:08.504 --> 34:10.798
there won't be atmosphere changes
till tomorrow.

34:10.882 --> 34:12.633
It's gonna probably stay hot
from the heat island.

34:12.717 --> 34:14.093
It'll be hot again during the day.

34:14.177 --> 34:18.056
Anyway, seems like it'll be constant
and steady weather till next shift.

34:18.639 --> 34:19.766
I believe you should go.

34:22.518 --> 34:24.187
I promise I'll handle things
till you're back.

34:31.069 --> 34:32.028
You don't trust me?

34:33.613 --> 34:37.075
You trust that we'll do our best
on the work that you assign us, don't you?

34:38.701 --> 34:40.119
You know that I trust you.

34:40.620 --> 34:43.289
It's my job, though.
It's my job to oversee the team.

34:43.372 --> 34:45.541
- It's not about--
- Everyone here knows what you must do.

34:45.625 --> 34:47.293
How much you care about everything.

34:47.376 --> 34:50.546
But your responsibility now
is to be a good daughter, so go.

34:54.967 --> 34:56.886
I owe you one. Please, go now.

35:03.309 --> 35:04.435
We'll be fine.

35:07.605 --> 35:09.774
Tell me you'll call
if something happens, okay?

35:16.823 --> 35:18.074
Mr. Lee.

35:18.825 --> 35:19.992
Come on.

35:20.076 --> 35:21.661
Yeah. Coming, sir.

35:42.473 --> 35:44.058
What happened? How is she?

35:46.936 --> 35:48.062
I don't know.

35:48.146 --> 35:50.022
They took blood
and did an X-ray, that's all.

35:51.232 --> 35:53.609
She said she felt weak
and had to lie down.

35:53.693 --> 35:55.194
She kept saying she was dizzy.

35:56.362 --> 35:58.030
She kept throwing up if she tried to eat.

35:58.114 --> 36:00.408
And then she got up to go to the bathroom,

36:01.909 --> 36:05.121
she lost her balance
and hit her head when she went down.

36:07.707 --> 36:11.502
And her… her forehead
was bleeding so much blood.

36:12.712 --> 36:16.674
I really thought that she could've died
right there and you weren't here!

36:22.930 --> 36:24.098
What were the test results?

36:25.975 --> 36:27.643
There aren't any yet.

36:27.727 --> 36:32.064
There are so many other patients today
that everything's taking longer.

36:51.709 --> 36:52.668
Mr. Um.

36:52.752 --> 36:54.754
- Here's the data you wanted.
- Wow.

36:55.421 --> 36:57.590
All right, could you check
Seoul's ground-surface temperature

36:57.673 --> 36:59.926
and radiation
every ten minutes or so, please?

37:00.009 --> 37:01.093
Yes, of course.

37:02.261 --> 37:04.347
You're keeping an eye
on the anticyclone's path, right?

37:04.430 --> 37:08.100
Yeah. I really don't think
it'll change anytime soon.

37:08.184 --> 37:10.311
Hm, then let me know
if it speeds up at all.

37:10.394 --> 37:11.479
Yes, sir.

37:26.410 --> 37:29.664
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

37:39.715 --> 37:40.925
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

37:51.310 --> 37:53.062
Did you make it
to the hospital okay?

38:17.545 --> 38:18.629
What am I gonna do?

38:29.181 --> 38:30.016
Jin…

38:31.183 --> 38:32.727
JIN HA-KYUNG

38:38.441 --> 38:40.151
I can't.

39:01.797 --> 39:04.967
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

39:05.676 --> 39:06.927
Good morning.

39:07.011 --> 39:09.180
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

39:31.994 --> 39:33.537
Where is she?

39:33.621 --> 39:35.831
Did she call out? Is she gonna be late?

39:38.125 --> 39:39.835
Oh, no. No.

39:44.173 --> 39:45.966
I thought it went well.

39:46.050 --> 39:47.259
Han? What brings you here?

39:47.343 --> 39:48.511
Goodness.

39:48.594 --> 39:50.846
Have you been here all night?

39:50.930 --> 39:52.390
I was. There was so much work to do.

39:52.473 --> 39:53.307
Yeah.

39:53.391 --> 39:56.519
Oh, and, uh, I didn't see
Director Jin come out.

39:56.602 --> 39:57.812
Where is she?

39:57.895 --> 39:59.772
Well, she had to leave for her reasons.

39:59.855 --> 40:01.315
Oh, reasons.

40:01.399 --> 40:04.360
Why do you need the director
so early after the shift's over?

40:05.152 --> 40:07.905
It's not particularly important.
Don't worry about it.

40:09.198 --> 40:11.242
- I'm getting hangover soup. Any takers?
- Ooh.

40:11.325 --> 40:12.493
- Hey.
- I'll go.

40:12.576 --> 40:13.452
- Sounds good.
- Yes.

40:13.536 --> 40:15.287
- Let's go.
- Enjoy your food, everyone.

40:15.371 --> 40:16.747
- Thanks.
- Bye.

40:23.129 --> 40:25.172
How am I supposed
to get this done in time?

40:26.340 --> 40:28.968
Why does he come to our department
so much all of a sudden?

40:29.051 --> 40:32.304
Yeah, it's weird. He's so smug.
Like we all don't know he's a cheater.

40:32.388 --> 40:33.222
It's gross.

40:33.305 --> 40:35.015
I feel like he's always there.

40:35.099 --> 40:37.268
It's 'cause he's desperate
and doesn't know what to do.

40:37.351 --> 40:38.436
Why is he desperate?

40:38.519 --> 40:40.354
- The column.
- His column?

40:40.438 --> 40:41.313
You mean,

40:42.106 --> 40:43.649
- the monthly story column?
- Mm.

40:43.732 --> 40:46.402
Director Jin ghost wrote
every single one, but he gets credit.

40:46.485 --> 40:48.529
Huh? But he gets credit?

40:48.612 --> 40:50.072
I'm sure lots of people know.

40:50.698 --> 40:52.241
You knew, right, Mr. Shin?

40:53.242 --> 40:54.577
See? Even he knew.

40:54.660 --> 40:57.913
Gosh. What a jerk. I hope he gets caught.

40:57.997 --> 41:02.209
Honestly, I think Director Jin
is a little softer than she could be.

41:02.751 --> 41:03.669
Mr. Shin?

41:07.173 --> 41:08.299
Doors opening.

41:11.135 --> 41:12.636
Uh, actually, I've gotta get home.

41:12.720 --> 41:14.305
Why? You're not in the mood for soup?

41:14.388 --> 41:16.682
No, I had a big lunch.
I'll see you next shift.

41:16.765 --> 41:17.641
- Okay.
- Bye.

41:17.725 --> 41:18.601
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

41:19.602 --> 41:21.562
Can we get some fish tonight
instead of the beef?

41:21.645 --> 41:23.481
- Sure. Sounds good.
- Sounds delicious.

41:23.564 --> 41:26.066
I clearly asked
for all the meteorological day scripts.

41:26.150 --> 41:27.818
What part of that didn't get through?

41:27.902 --> 41:29.737
Who told you to summarize them?

41:29.820 --> 41:32.156
Well, since the details of
the Administrator's speech weren't…

41:32.239 --> 41:34.575
relevant for the part of planning,
I thought I'd save you time.

41:34.658 --> 41:36.368
No one told you to make that call.

41:36.452 --> 41:38.120
I'm the director.

41:38.954 --> 41:39.788
Uh, sorry, sir.

41:39.872 --> 41:42.500
I'm getting tired
of these mistakes.

41:43.751 --> 41:45.169
Fix it by tomorrow.

42:00.559 --> 42:01.685
Mr. Shin.

42:19.161 --> 42:20.246
Here.

42:21.580 --> 42:22.414
Did you eat?

42:22.498 --> 42:25.751
Of course, I had breakfast with the kids.
The soup you made was good.

42:25.834 --> 42:27.378
Huh, the kids made it to school?

42:27.461 --> 42:28.712
Yeah. Of course.

42:32.341 --> 42:34.593
You know our son wants
to start art classes.

42:35.928 --> 42:39.056
English, math, taekwondo,
and art to top it off?

42:41.433 --> 42:44.061
It's gonna be 800,000,
900,000 won a month.

42:46.105 --> 42:47.940
And do the same thing for our other son.

42:49.066 --> 42:50.734
Yeah. I know.

42:57.866 --> 42:59.243
You think just one year is enough?

43:01.161 --> 43:03.664
'Cause I can't do longer than that
by myself.

43:04.707 --> 43:05.874
Myung-ju.

43:07.668 --> 43:09.837
If you can promise me
you'll be working again in a year,

43:09.920 --> 43:12.006
even if you don't pass the exam,

43:12.673 --> 43:16.051
if you'll promise,
then I can hold on for a year.

43:20.681 --> 43:21.974
Oh…

43:25.060 --> 43:28.355
How'd you get so lucky
to get me for a wife?

43:30.941 --> 43:32.151
I wish I knew.

43:32.943 --> 43:34.486
I'm the luckiest.

43:38.782 --> 43:40.659
I promise, honey.

43:41.660 --> 43:43.537
And I promise I'll pass the test.

43:51.545 --> 43:53.339
Just look at you, my husband.

43:53.964 --> 43:55.591
So many tears are falling.

43:56.884 --> 43:58.552
I know.

44:03.015 --> 44:04.433
The coffee is wonderful.

44:48.519 --> 44:50.646
She's extremely dehydrated.

44:50.729 --> 44:54.316
Her hemoglobin levels are much lower
than I'd like to see.

44:54.400 --> 44:56.568
Her electrolytes are expectedly low, too.

44:57.903 --> 45:00.322
So we've given her
some fluids intravenously,

45:00.406 --> 45:01.740
and she's got a prescription.

45:01.824 --> 45:03.909
She needs to finish her IV,
and then she'll be good to go.

45:04.702 --> 45:07.037
So she doesn't need
to stay here overnight?

45:07.121 --> 45:08.622
You can take her home.

45:08.706 --> 45:11.250
Just make sure she's eating,
and she needs rest.

45:12.042 --> 45:14.420
Right now, she needs to keep
stress levels down.

45:14.503 --> 45:16.422
I hope you and your sister
can help with that.

45:17.005 --> 45:18.549
It's our responsibility to our parents.

45:19.550 --> 45:21.009
Okay. Thank you.

45:28.142 --> 45:30.978
She's dehydrated.
But she can come home.

45:31.061 --> 45:34.189
We can take care of her.
She needs to relax.

45:34.273 --> 45:35.149
You hear that?

45:38.026 --> 45:39.737
- It wasn't about me.
- You stressed her out.

45:39.820 --> 45:41.113
It's about my work.

45:41.822 --> 45:44.116
- I'm a director now. It's different.
- Be quiet.

45:44.199 --> 45:46.243
Look who's feeling better now.

45:48.412 --> 45:51.540
- I'm so glad you're here.
- Mom's smiling.

46:02.050 --> 46:05.846
MOTEL

46:16.732 --> 46:18.025
Ten million won.

46:18.650 --> 46:21.111
This is all that I have.
This is the last time, okay?

46:21.695 --> 46:23.113
All that I have, I've given you.

46:26.200 --> 46:27.659
I knew it.

46:28.535 --> 46:31.997
Your girlfriend's better
at opening your wallet than I'll ever be.

46:33.040 --> 46:34.249
Right?

46:34.333 --> 46:37.419
Director Jin Ha-kyung. I know everything.

46:39.046 --> 46:41.256
She's obviously on the old side.

46:41.340 --> 46:43.133
She's awful pretty, though.

46:43.717 --> 46:46.428
She looks all delicate.
A real classy type.

46:46.512 --> 46:50.432
By the way, how far up
the ladder as a director at the KMA?

46:50.516 --> 46:52.309
I bet her paycheck's high.

46:52.392 --> 46:53.936
I get it.

46:54.019 --> 46:56.647
You're just like your old man.
Get a girl who'll take care of you.

46:56.730 --> 46:58.482
Right? I see you.

46:59.149 --> 47:02.945
Dad, you're saying you met
Director Jin in person?

47:06.657 --> 47:08.617
Well, didn't you come 'cause she said to?

47:11.411 --> 47:14.540
See, I really need money.

47:14.623 --> 47:16.291
And I needed it yesterday, right?

47:16.875 --> 47:18.919
Would you find it in your heart
to lend me any?

47:21.547 --> 47:25.092
'Cause my boy, Si-woo, he's great.
I love that kid.

47:25.676 --> 47:28.345
Well, except his cash.

47:28.971 --> 47:33.100
I guess if he gets switched to HQ,
he's not a total idiot.

47:33.183 --> 47:34.726
But he tells me he's still broke.

47:38.730 --> 47:43.360
I say that it's time for your investment
if you really like my boy.

47:44.111 --> 47:45.988
Ten million won should do it.

47:52.119 --> 47:53.871
You've actually lost it.

47:53.954 --> 47:55.581
What, it worked out.

47:56.540 --> 48:01.336
Hey. Hey, hey. In my eyes,
it just means she really does like you.

48:01.420 --> 48:04.673
She's loads better than that other chick.
Ugh, the reporter, the dumb one?

48:04.756 --> 48:06.466
I like this one better.

48:06.550 --> 48:10.012
And this one, she's so my style.

48:10.721 --> 48:13.599
Anyway, it means a lot, kid.
Here. Use this for a taxi.

48:17.019 --> 48:19.605
Disrespect.
You're gonna grab your old man?

48:19.688 --> 48:20.772
Let go!

48:20.856 --> 48:22.441
Why did you ruin everything?

48:22.524 --> 48:25.068
- What did I do?
- You ruined everything!

48:26.153 --> 48:27.863
You're ruining my life.

48:29.364 --> 48:30.449
Leave me alone.

48:32.034 --> 48:33.869
Please, please just stay away from me.

48:34.494 --> 48:35.871
Stay away.

48:46.757 --> 48:49.176
That asshole.

49:01.188 --> 49:03.774
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

49:11.865 --> 49:13.158
Mom.

49:21.416 --> 49:23.126
Have some food before you go.

49:23.210 --> 49:24.544
Don't worry, Mom.

49:24.628 --> 49:26.630
There's bulgogi and radish kimchi.

49:27.339 --> 49:30.092
It's what Tae-kyung brought you
when she stopped by the other day.

49:30.175 --> 49:31.134
Have you had any?

49:34.429 --> 49:37.015
What? Did you get it
from the guy upstairs?

49:37.599 --> 49:38.642
What are you saying?

49:38.725 --> 49:41.561
I had to. You changed the door code
and don't answer your phone.

49:41.645 --> 49:43.522
You should have left it at the front desk.

49:44.272 --> 49:45.148
I…

49:45.232 --> 49:48.402
It would've gone bad.
You can't leave bulgogi out.

49:48.485 --> 49:50.862
Enough. Stop. It's all right.

49:51.446 --> 49:53.949
I need a glass of water.

49:54.908 --> 49:58.328
Mm.

50:01.248 --> 50:02.666
Her neighbors are weird.

50:02.749 --> 50:05.043
Why wouldn't he call and give it to her?

50:06.586 --> 50:07.754
Seemed like he lived alone.

50:07.838 --> 50:09.548
No.

50:09.631 --> 50:11.341
The pig ate it on his own?

50:16.054 --> 50:18.849
DOES IT SMELL?
NATURAL MINERAL PRESERVATIVE

50:35.365 --> 50:37.617
CALLING
APARTMENT 1201

50:38.577 --> 50:42.497
How in the hell is this woman
still not home? It's been days!

50:43.915 --> 50:46.043
You're not gonna realize
your food is missing?

50:48.086 --> 50:50.964
How long do I have to keep it?
I'll toss it someday!

50:51.923 --> 50:54.092
It all stinks!

51:08.190 --> 51:09.983
Tae-kyung, get Mom's water.

51:48.647 --> 51:49.689
Is Han Ki-jun here?

51:50.774 --> 51:53.110
I don't know.
I haven't seen him yet today.

51:54.986 --> 51:57.280
I hope he finished.

52:03.870 --> 52:05.038
What do I do?

52:06.039 --> 52:07.124
What do I do?

52:08.416 --> 52:09.668
I'll get fired.

52:10.836 --> 52:12.003
I don't know.

52:16.424 --> 52:18.802
Ha-kyung, it's me.

52:18.885 --> 52:22.097
I'm sorry, but can you help me
with the column last time?

52:22.889 --> 52:26.852
Damn it! Are you crazy?

52:26.935 --> 52:29.729
Come on. Come on. Come on.
I can't text her. I can't.

52:29.813 --> 52:32.399
No, I shouldn't. Oh, what do I do?

52:32.482 --> 52:33.942
What do I do?

52:34.025 --> 52:35.652
I have to… I have to call her.

52:36.403 --> 52:37.487
Damn it.

52:42.784 --> 52:44.035
Oh, Ha-kyung, hey.

52:45.495 --> 52:47.706
How's night shift treating you?
You must be tired.

52:49.040 --> 52:50.959
Uh, I called, because…

52:55.881 --> 52:57.465
You have to save me.

52:58.925 --> 53:00.302
I'm sorry, I am.

53:01.094 --> 53:05.849
One last time, save me.
Can you do the column, huh?

53:35.587 --> 53:37.964
So, how's your mom doing?

53:39.174 --> 53:40.717
She's well. Thank you.

53:41.718 --> 53:42.844
That's good news.

53:50.894 --> 53:52.103
I'm so sorry.

53:52.187 --> 53:53.021
For what?

53:56.191 --> 53:57.192
For my dad.

54:01.238 --> 54:02.489
I had no idea.

54:07.327 --> 54:09.412
I can't even say how sorry I am.

54:10.538 --> 54:11.623
Are you hungry?

54:19.923 --> 54:20.882
Go ahead.

54:21.925 --> 54:24.010
My mom always makes it from scratch.

54:25.303 --> 54:28.181
It's a tradition for us.
We make it in the summer every year.

54:29.557 --> 54:30.392
Why?

54:31.851 --> 54:33.895
It's almost the anniversary
of my dad's death,

54:34.896 --> 54:36.523
and this was his favorite thing to eat.

54:49.953 --> 54:51.371
Mmm…

54:53.039 --> 54:55.417
This is actually good.
I guess Ha-kyung's a chef like you.

54:55.500 --> 54:57.961
If you forget she complained
the whole time, it's great.

54:59.129 --> 55:00.422
Is she gonna visit?

55:01.881 --> 55:02.716
What do you think?

55:03.550 --> 55:04.968
Don't hold your breath.

55:05.051 --> 55:06.845
You know how she is about work.

55:12.726 --> 55:14.019
You're right, she did well.

55:17.605 --> 55:21.401
The day my father died
is probably the day

55:22.152 --> 55:24.195
I'd most like to erase from my memory.

55:28.575 --> 55:30.160
I'm back. Hello?

55:38.168 --> 55:39.294
Mama?

55:51.806 --> 55:53.308
Is anybody home?

56:27.592 --> 56:29.803
His business went under
and it hit him hard.

56:31.054 --> 56:33.932
He took it so hard
that he thought he had to disappear.

56:43.400 --> 56:45.735
So that's where I'm at with my dad.

56:47.320 --> 56:51.991
So you don't have to worry
that I'll judge you at all with your dad.

56:53.868 --> 56:58.206
"When one cloud meets another,
there's a great noise, thunder.

56:58.289 --> 57:00.792
Like them, I want to meet you,

57:01.459 --> 57:04.963
shouting about it from the rooftops
without a thought."

57:23.398 --> 57:24.816
It's really good.

57:28.111 --> 57:30.697
"When one cloud
suddenly meets another cloud,

57:30.780 --> 57:33.366
There's a great light, too, lightning.

57:33.450 --> 57:35.118
With that light when I meet you,

57:35.952 --> 57:38.830
I'll see the path
I strayed from long ago."

57:40.165 --> 57:41.583
Can you promise me one thing?

57:47.589 --> 57:48.423
What is it?

57:49.966 --> 57:51.926
If things change
and you don't want to be with me,

57:52.802 --> 57:54.304
I want to be the first to know.

57:55.430 --> 57:58.475
Even if you're having doubts,
don't be afraid to let me know.

58:02.103 --> 58:04.731
I know I'd be heartbroken
if your feelings changed

58:04.814 --> 58:05.648
and we called it off.

58:05.732 --> 58:07.275
But it hurts even more…

58:09.235 --> 58:11.279
if I don't see it coming at all.

58:14.574 --> 58:15.658
That happened with him.

58:24.709 --> 58:26.294
And with Ki-jun, too.

58:32.133 --> 58:34.719
Tell me that I won't be surprised by you.

58:37.430 --> 58:40.099
"You shine brightly
when you tell me…

58:40.975 --> 58:45.396
that rain needs to meet another rain
for them to get drenched."

58:47.398 --> 58:48.399
I promise you.

58:50.818 --> 58:51.986
Okay, good.

58:58.535 --> 58:59.953
Well, then let's live together.

59:04.999 --> 59:06.042
THEMED STORY FOR JULY

59:06.125 --> 59:07.585
Ready to print.

59:08.253 --> 59:09.295
Let's see.

59:10.088 --> 59:12.715
Assistant Director Kim did decent work.

59:12.799 --> 59:15.677
And I hope you consider his column,
just consider mine, too.

59:15.760 --> 59:17.220
I'll respect whichever you pick.

59:17.303 --> 59:18.763
Okay, very good.

59:18.846 --> 59:19.847
Okay.

59:25.144 --> 59:26.312
Good work.

59:26.896 --> 59:29.107
I should really be saying that to you.

59:30.358 --> 59:32.902
I did wanna warn you the director
has a habit of thinking

59:32.986 --> 59:35.029
things need to change
when he just needs to relax.

59:35.113 --> 59:36.197
Huh?

59:36.739 --> 59:38.783
Oh, yeah.
Well, at least I got the experience.

59:38.866 --> 59:41.703
That's right, you did.
And you're gonna go far.

59:41.786 --> 59:43.538
You did well, for sure.

59:43.621 --> 59:47.125
Ah, the mighty Han Ki-jun is back.

59:47.208 --> 59:48.835
I want this sent
to the printer right away.

59:48.918 --> 59:51.671
Yes, I'll do it now.
I'll send the column myself.

59:53.047 --> 59:56.259
I knew it was still in there.

01:00:08.980 --> 01:00:11.149
WILL YOU BE LATE?
I THINK SO. YOU CAN GO TO BED FIRST.

01:00:11.232 --> 01:00:13.067
Can we meet up for a sec?

01:00:14.694 --> 01:00:15.778
Hm…

01:00:20.908 --> 01:00:23.036
What's going on? I'm sure you're busy.

01:00:23.828 --> 01:00:25.163
You want a drink? It's on me.

01:00:26.789 --> 01:00:29.459
Anyway, were you able to register us?

01:00:29.542 --> 01:00:31.669
If we're all set,
then we can look into the loan.

01:00:31.753 --> 01:00:33.504
We don't have much longer
in the apartment.

01:00:34.213 --> 01:00:37.216
Well, that's kinda
what I wanted to talk about.

01:00:37.884 --> 01:00:38.968
Ah, what's up?

01:00:40.803 --> 01:00:45.433
I wanna hold off
on officially registering anything.

01:00:47.894 --> 01:00:48.895
Huh?

01:00:52.899 --> 01:00:56.069
You think I should live with you?

01:00:56.653 --> 01:00:59.530
Mm-hm. It'll make me so happy.

01:01:01.240 --> 01:01:03.493
You could live here. Say you will.

01:01:08.373 --> 01:01:10.083
What do you mean, hold off?

01:01:10.875 --> 01:01:11.834
Wait.

01:01:12.543 --> 01:01:14.128
What are you saying right now?

01:01:14.212 --> 01:01:16.005
Why would you want to put it off?

01:01:17.048 --> 01:01:19.550
Why? Because of me?

01:01:22.178 --> 01:01:23.971
I just think it would be smart.

01:02:05.304 --> 01:02:09.392
Today, we can expect to have
over 0.3ppm ozone concentration.

01:02:09.475 --> 01:02:12.478
The weather is perfectly fine.
What's with the ozone warning?

01:02:12.562 --> 01:02:15.022
Who is handling the complaint calls
that came into Team Two today?

01:02:15.106 --> 01:02:16.733
I didn't do all that work in school

01:02:16.816 --> 01:02:19.277
only to come here at work
in a call center.

01:02:19.986 --> 01:02:22.655
We are here to do that kind of work.

01:02:23.698 --> 01:02:24.741
Go ahead if you want.

01:02:24.824 --> 01:02:26.200
- Huh?
- Divorce.

01:02:26.284 --> 01:02:28.911
Haven't you heard
they're living in the night-duty room?

01:02:29.454 --> 01:02:31.330
Did you just say both of them?

01:02:32.415 --> 01:02:33.666
Lee Si-woo…

01:02:34.542 --> 01:02:37.211
Her husband works
at the KMA, you know?

01:02:38.588 --> 01:02:42.592
I think Ki-jun found out
that you and I lived together.
